<title>PORTUGAL: Yield rises on Portuguese 364-day bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Portuguese 364-day bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield rose to 5.6513 percent, from 5.5913 percent previously, at the Institute of Public Credit Management's (IGCP) sale of 364-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The IGCP placed 16 billion escudos of the 20 billion on offer. The maximum rate rose to 5.68 percent from 5.60 percent previously. --LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
